[Music]  this is a typical eighteenth-century  manor house it's also the home of Barry  null the building contractor lived for  many years in Switzerland before he  returned to his native land good morning  welcome to my house do come in  a century ago this was the residence of  the bailiff of Jersey the islands top  administrator today it offers space  enough for Barry Knowles two daughters  and their families  [Music]  we love the grounds because a beautiful  outside garden I think that loved this  entrance hall and just to share space of  the various rooms it was better than  anything else be could find when we  moved back so we we looked at dozen  houses and this was our favorite by far  the family only uses the dining room for  special occasions daughter Jasmine  decided on the interior design it was  her idea to paint the wood paneling a  light color it gives everything a fresh  look before all the wood was original  and orange and then the walls were just  the white wallpaper but I stripped them  all back and doing that I found some of  the original wallpaper so then I chose  to go with a similar wallpaper that I  liked a new one but quite floral and  natural the wallpaper comes from a  collection that's based on design  patterns from the British Museum  [Music]  the fireplace is original the family  take their meals in the adjacent kitchen  [Music]  the chandeliers in the living room may  be a bit uber posh otherwise subdued  shades dominate  [Music]  when we first moved in it was very regal  and grand and there was a lot of gold  and red which we don't really like and  we didn't feel very at home here so we  just tried to neutralize it and make it  a lot lighter and fresher cleaner and  just more homely this is my favorite  wallpaper it's from Andrew Martin and  it's of love letters from the second  world war but I had a big argument with  my dad choosing it because he wanted he  didn't really want it in here and I  wanted the whole room to be like this so  we compromised and I have one little  wall with it but I think it would have  looked better if it had been everywhere  the living room looks out onto the  conservatory which is where the family  prefer to spend their time when Barry  wants some quiet he withdraws to the  smoking-room jasmine did the interior  design in there too just as everywhere  else in the house the walls are trimmed  with the work of his favorite artist  Edmund Blum p-well Edmund bump is the  most famous of Jersey artists so it fits  into an old jersey house very nicely we  like his work both etchings oil  paintings watercolors sand it's quite  fun tried to collect them at various  auctions around the world there are 800  square meters in the 10 room house all  the bedrooms are on the first and second  floors the maze-like hallways create a  feeling of intimacy and privacy  [Music]  now this is the only one we really kept  the same because I just love the high  ceilings and the neutral colors and I  love the bed that was here when we  bought the house and it just makes me  feel like a princess in here a separate  bath and dressing room emphasized the  luxurious style of the house  [Music]  at 10,000 square meters the garden is  huge it provides plenty of protection  from prying eyes when we came back to to  Jersey we just came in through the gates  of the driveway we just we just loved  what we saw and they got just got better  from there onwards we went inside we  loved the inside so we decided that was  the house for us in fact it's now a home  for three generations and it's managed  to hold on to its old-time charm even  after its modern facelift  [Music]

